nges but does **not** rewrite scoring;\n- one authoritative terminal kill;\n- Don remains outside routine pipeline control. memcite\n\nEC4 gave us some useful hardening—source validation/data floor, auditability/provenance, bounded concurrency, stale-line refresh/kill, explicit failure rendering—but the mistake was letting the later build blend **Quant, committees, convergence, and gatekeeping** into one architecture. We do not carry that forward. memcite\n\nFor D2: locked conceptually. **AI Convergence gets the MGM line we actually bet.** Multi-book/consensus belongs to Quant or upstream market intelligence, not this reasoning engine.\n\nFor D3, I want Luce to recover the actual EC3 prompt philosophy before we touch the build.\n\n:::writing{variant=\"standard\" id=\"64173\" title=\"P14 — Luce EC3 Prompt and Gatekeeper Recovery\"}\n**[P14] LUCE — EC3 PROMPT / GATEKEEPER RECOVERY**\n\n**Objective:** Recover the original EC3 AI decision methodology and prompt architecture so Don/Coda can use it as the philosophical base for the new EdgeCrew AI Convergence design.\n\n**Do not redesign. Do not mutate. Do not assume EC4 is authoritative.**\n\n### SEARCH SCOPE\nLocate the strongest surviving EC3 artifacts, prompts, routers, outputs, and lineage evidence across the known EdgeCrew/project/history surfaces.\n\n### RECOVER\n\n**[A] EC3 PROCESS**\nReconstruct the original ordered flow from data/slate through final output.\n\n**[B] ANALYST PROMPTS**\nIdentify the actual EC3 sport/model prompts and extract:\n- analyst role\n- required inputs\n- reasoning objective\n- output fields\n- grading/confidence structure\n- key_factors / red_flags\n- independence requirements\n\nDo not dump full prompt text unless necessary; summarize structure and cite paths.\n\n**[C] CONVERGENCE**\nDetermine exactly:\n- where independent lanes first meet\n- what convergence was allowed to do\n- whether it blended scores, selected signals, or synthesized reasoning\n- how picks were produced afterward\n\n**[D] KIMI GATEKEEPER**\nRecover Kimi’s original gatekeeper philosophy:\n- inputs received\n- checks performed\n- authority\n- prohibited actions\n- challenge / flag / verify / escalate behavior\n- terminal KILL behavior\n- relationship to Don\n\n**[E] HARD RULES / DATA FLOOR**\nRecover EC3 rules for:\n- missing data\n- stale odds\n- source/data validity\n- EV/hard-rule checks\n- kill-switch behavior\n\n**[F] EC4 CARRY-FORWARD CANDIDATES**\nIdentify only EC4 improvements that strengthen EC3 without importing EC4’s combined Quant/convergence architecture.\n\nClassify each:\n`KEEP / REJECT / NEEDS DON-CODA REVIEW`\n\nExplicitly evaluate:\n- source validation\n- data floor\n- provenance/audit trail\n- bounded concurrency\n- stale-line refresh/kill\n- FAIL-only rendering\n- committee constructs\n- consensus bonuses\n- Quant layers\n- multi-book logic\n\n**[G] CONTAMINATION CHECK**\nFlag any EC3 artifact that appears later modified by EC4/EC8 assumptions.\n\n**[H] MINIMUM RECOVERED PHILOSOPHY**\nReturn the smallest coherent set of principles sufficient to rebuild AI Convergence from EC3.\n\n**STATUS:** PASS / CONFLICT / UNKNOWN  \n**CONFIDENCE:** %\n\nNO MUTATIONS.\n:::\n\nThat is the right next move. We recover **what EC3 actually was**, not what later EdgeCrew documents say it became.\n\n**SESSION FOOTER**\n- STATUS: PROCEED\n- D1: frozen/delivered data estate — aligned\n- D2: MGM line only for AI Convergence — aligned\n- D3: pending EC3 prompt/gatekeeper recovery\n- D4: hold until recovered architecture is clear\n- CURRENT ROUTE: P14 Luce\n- IMPLEMENTATION: HOLD\n- DON INPUT NEEDED: NO until P14 returns", "text_chars": 4308, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "empty_text_parts": 0, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "189fc496-5042-438e-836d-709d90015dc6", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1789687635.951178, "updated_at": null, "statu