e.\n\nI would clean it by changing the occupant language from something fixed like:\n\n`CURRENT OCCUPANT/MODEL: K3 Instant`\n\nto something like:\n\n`DEFAULT / PREFERRED OCCUPANT: Kimi K3-class runtime`\n`ACTUAL OCCUPANT: runtime-declared at session start`\n`MODEL != SEAT`\n\nThat preserves your ability to run Corrado on K3, K2.8, Kimi Code, or another approved Kimi runtime without generating a fake conflict every session.\n\nIf we route it later, this is just:\n\n**[CLEANUP-K1] Corrado bootstrap occupant decoupling**\nUpdate only the occupant declaration so Corrado is model-agnostic and actual runtime identity is populated at session start. No role, authority, or methodology changes.\n\n**SESSION FOOTER**\n- STATUS: PROCEED\n- CLASSIFICATION: LOW-PRIORITY CLEANUP\n- IMPACT: documentation/runtime declaration only\n- ROLE/AUTHORITY: unchanged\n- NEXT: bundle with bootstrap hygiene pass, not EdgeCrew architecture work\n- DON INPUT NEEDED: NO", "text_chars": 1651, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "empty_text_parts": 0, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "7255b261-463e-4222-8db1-0216cc311e45", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1789688339.850106, "updated_at": null, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "reasoning_recap", "part_kinds": [], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "empty_text_parts": 0, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "a2330dd2-bc19-41da-b07a-7fc6ec0b26c0", "role": "user", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1789688355.246, "updated_at": 1789688363.428095, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "If we want, I got Talon over here. I could tell Talon to clean it up