phical core:\n\n**deterministic lane + independent AI reasoning + one convergence point + gatekeeper + human decision.**\n\nWhat EC4 did was pull two separate disciplines into the same stack:\n- **Quant** = data/market/statistical methodology\n- **Convergence** = reasoning/decision methodology\n\nOnce those got coupled too tightly, Quant started shaping the convergence architecture instead of just feeding it evidence.\n\nWhat we’re doing now is separating them again:\n\n**Quant produces/supports evidence.**  \n**Convergence reasons over the frozen evidence.**  \n**Kimi validates.**  \n**Don decides.**\n\nThat’s much closer to where you left EC3, just with better contracts, provenance, failure handling, and runtime discipline.\n\nSo I would not characterize this as “we lost EdgeCrew.” It’s more like **EC4 over-composed two good methodologies into one system**, and now we’re decomposing them back into the correct boundaries.\n\n**SESSION FOOTER**\n- STATUS: PROCEED\n- METHODOLOGY RECOVERY: on track\n- QUANT: separated as supporting methodology\n- CONVERGENCE: restored as independent reasoning methodology\n- NEXT: finish Corrado challenge, then reconcile through Luce only where needed\n- DON INPUT NEEDED: NO", "text_chars": 1585, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "empty_text_parts": 0, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "03df768d-94f4-4d92-97c4-b281e7f93591", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1789688408.523564, "updated_at": null, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "reasoning_recap", "part_kinds": [], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "empty_text_parts": 0, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "10267e9b-d43f-4f37-bed7-7466614f06d0", "role": "user", "rol