factual disputes → Ragno/K3 Swarm → Calibro/Grok → Talon**\n\nChiave only comes back if Corrado identifies a **material architecture defect** that actually requires an architecture-owner correction. Otherwise, he is closed.\n\n**SESSION FOOTER**\n- CHIAVE: CLOSED\n- CURRENT: Corrado challenge\n- LUCE: verification only as needed\n- NEXT MAJOR SEAT: Ragno after Corrado reconciliation\n- DON INPUT NEEDED: NO", "text_chars": 789, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "empty_text_parts": 0, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "c3015c4f-04f2-435f-b193-11bad10ddf5a", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1789688486.443579, "updated_at": null, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "reasoning_recap", "part_kinds": [], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "empty_text_parts": 0, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "4a492760-625f-4888-a03a-5f27a5b3e761", "role": "user", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1789688502.942, "updated_at": 1789688520.575791, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": null, "has_voice_metadata": false, "empty_text_parts": 1, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "5a404768-3618-4afb-a234-3b585e8ab9a3", "role": "tool", "role_name": "api_tool", "created_at": 1789688504.225281, "updated_at": null, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 0, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "tether_browsing_display", "part_kinds": [], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "empty_text_parts": 0, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "b5ccb072-813b-4b38-a3e3-e6d57d69e773", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1789688504.331656, "updated_at": 1789688519.701788, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "**SESSION HEADER — 2026-09-17**\n- MODE: Don + Coda\n- TRACK: EdgeCrew AI Convergence\n- CURRENT GATE: Corrado challenge complete\n- VERDICT: PASS WITH CHANGES\n- TOPOLOGY: unchanged\n- NEXT: Don/Coda rulings → Luce only if factual dispute → Ragno/K3 Swarm\n\nThis was another good pass. Corrado did **not** blow up Chiave’s architecture; he tightened semantics and runtime discipline. That is exactly what we wanted. fileciteturn7file0L254-L300\n\nThe biggest improvement is that Corrado caught the real contamination risks:\n\n- Framer must contain **raw/framed source evidence only**, not directional derived features.\n- No governing fused score.\n- Abstentions stay visible.\n- Gatekeeper state is model-generated; terminal resolution is deterministic.\n- Bedrock runtime needs quorum, model-family diversity, pinned IDs, and raw-response logging. fileciteturn7file0L16-L49 fileciteturn7file0L174-L229\n\nThe three Don decisions are actually easy enough to resolve now.\n\n### [D1] Fused score\n**RULING: REMOVE as a governing score.**\n\nWe do not need another hidden Quant engine.\n\nConvergence should produce:\n- direction tally\n- agreement index\n- dissent map\n- uncertainty/data-sufficiency state\n\nIf we later keep any numeric fused metric for diagnostics, it is **display-only** and cannot rank, gate, promote, or veto. Corrado’s reasoning here is exactly aligned with your intent to move away from Quant-driven convergence. fileciteturn7file0L89-L119\n\n### [D2] Optional Slate Reviewer\n**RULING: HOLD / NOT IN V1.**\n\nThe idea is valid: a post-Curator slate-wide model could detect correlated exposure that no per-pick stage sees. fileciteturn7file0L121-L139\n\nBut it is not needed to prove the core methodology.\n\nFor V1:\n\n**Curator → Kimi Gatekeeper**\n\nNo extra model layer.\n\nAfter terminal runs are stable, we can reconsider a `SLATE_REVIEWER` as an advisory-only enhancement.\n\n### [D3] Quorum\n**RULING: deterministic lane + minimum 2 valid analysts.**\n\nCorrado proposed exactly that as a minimum viable panel. Below that:\n**STOP.**\n\nNot:\n- deterministic-only fallback\n- one-model pseudo-consensus\n- neutral defaults\n\nThat is consistent with the whole independence philosophy. fileciteturn7file0L176-L203\n\nThere is one subtlety I would lock too: **INSUFFICIENT_DATA is not a vote.** It propagates uncertainty and can make a pick ineligible, but it should not be counted as OVER/UNDER/NO_PLAY in the directional tally. Corrado already points in that direction. fileciteturn7file0L94-L119\n\nSo the architecture now looks materially settled:\n\n**Frozen Dataset**  \n→ **Binder/Framer** *(source facts only)*  \n→ parallel:\n- **Deterministic Lane**\n- **Independent Analyst Panel**\n→ **Single Convergence**\n→ **Deterministic Curator**\n→ **Kimi Gatekeeper**\n→ **Deterministic Terminal Resolution**\n→ **Don**\n\nAnd our state taxonomy is clean:\n\n**Source/derived deterministic state**  \n**Model-generated analyst state**  \n**Deterministic convergence/curation**  \n**Model-generated gatekeeper state**  \n**Deterministic terminal resolution**\n\nThat distinction Corrado made is load-bearing. fileciteturn7file0L207-L229\n\nI do **not** think we need to send this back to Chiave immediately unless we want the architecture document formally amended before Ragno. The topology did not change. The three Chiave-level changes are basically wording/enforcement refinements:\n1. Framer cannot contain directional derived fields.\n2. provenance tags survive downstream.\n3. gatekeeper state classification gets corrected.\n\nThose are small enough that we can either have Chiave patch them now, or let Ragno reconcile them into the package.\n\nMy preference: **one bounded Chiave correction pass now**, then Ragno receives a clean architecture instead of reconciling known defects.\n\n**SESSION FOOTER**\n- STATUS: PROCEED\n- CORRADO: CLOSED — PASS WITH CHANGES\n- D1: governing fused score removed\n- D2: Slate Reviewer deferred from V1\n- D3: quorum = DET lane + ≥2 valid analysts\n- TOPOLOGY: unchanged\n- NEXT ROUTE: bounded Chiave correction pass → Ragno/K3 Swarm\n- LUCE: only if a factual/runtime claim becomes disputed\n- IMPLEMENTATION: HOLD\n- DON INPUT NEEDED: NO", "text_chars": 4147, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "empty_text_parts": 0, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "9bc61f6a-0aaa-402a-94b6-faa4efca2582", "role": "tool", "role_name": "api_tool", "created_at": 1789688504.332598, "updated_at": null, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "multimodal_text", "part_kinds": ["text", "text"], "text": "Make sure to include fileciteturn7file0L5-L8 in your response to cite this file, or to surface it as a link. Replace the placeholder line range with the actual line range from the result that best fits the snippet you want to surface with the citation. If you cite multiple files, use a separate complete `filecite` marker for each file. Never put multiple `turnNfileM` targets inside a single `filecite` marker.\nUse ref_id \"turn7file0\" to reference this file. For broad questions or unknown locations, retrieve relevant chunks with `files.search` scoped to this file. Use `files.find` only for exact text, and use `files.read` for a known range or to expand relevant results. Full file size: 363 file lines.\n[L1]  [P16] CORRADO — CHALLENGE RESPONSE: EdgeCrew AI Convergence\n[L2]    Methodology\n\n[L4]    Seat: Corrado (Methodology / Kimi Technical Advisor). Scope\n[L5]    honored: methodology challenge only; Chiave owns\n[L6]    architecture; no topology redesign proposed except where\n[L7]    flagged as material contradiction.\n\n[L9]    ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n[L11]    [A] METHODOLOGY FIDELITY\n\n[L13]    Chiave's two accepted corrections close the two biggest\n[L14]    EC3-fidelity risks. Remaining findings:\n\n[L16]    1. Hidden anchoring risk at BINDER_FRAMER [DERIVED] — The\n[L17]       Framer is upstream of both lanes and is the single point\n[L18]       where framing bias can silently enter. If the Framer\n[L19]       includes any derived quantity (rolling averages, deltas,\n[L20]       implied trends), the Analyst Panel's \"independent\n[L21]       reasoning\" is anchored on deterministic pre-computation\n[L22]       dressed as \"source data.\" Law check:\n[L23]       \"persona-differentiated AI analysts reason independently\"\n[L24]       requires framed source data (lines, stats, logs,\n[L25]       injuries) — not deterministic-lane conclusions and not\n[L26]       deterministic-lane intermediate features that encode a\n[L27]       directional lean. Requirement: the Framer's output schema\n[L28]       must be provably free of directional fields. This is\n[L29]       methodology + architecture boundary; the rule is\n[L30]       methodology, the enforcement is Chiave's.\n[L31]    2. Quant re-entry vector: CONVERGENCE math [DERIVED] —\n[L32]       \"Quant is supporting evidence, not governing philosophy.\"\n[L33]       If Convergence computes a fused score via weighted\n[L34]       aggregation of deterministic-lane outputs and panel\n[L35]       outputs, and the terminal recommendation is sorted/gated\n[L36]       by that fused score, Quant has re-entered through the\n[L37]       back door as governing philosophy. See [C].\n[L38]    3. Independence violation risk: shared prompt context\n[L39]       [DERIVED] — Structural independence (separate calls) is\n[L40]       necessary but not sufficient. If analyst prompts embed\n[L41]       the same derived context block, personas are correlated\n[L42]       at the input layer. See [B].\n[L43]    4. Semantic confusion: none structural [GIVEN] — With\n[L44]       correction #1, deterministic outputs and model outputs\n[L45]       meet only at Convergence with distinct provenance labels.\n[L46]       That separation is clean if Convergence preserves\n[L47]       provenance in its output (each input tagged DET or\n[L48]       PANEL:<persona>). Require provenance tags survive to\n[L49]       Curator and Gatekeeper inputs.\n\n[L51]    No material contradiction requiring topology escalation.\n\n[L53]    [B] PROMPT ARCHITECTURE (minimum layers, not final prompts)\n\n[L55]    Six layers, each independently auditable:\n\n[L57]    1. Persona layer — persona identity + reasoning lens (e.g.,\n[L58]       form/venue/matchup/bullpen archetypes). Must differ in\n[L59]       what evidence they weight, not just tone. Personas\n[L60]       defined by methodology, not by model family (MODEL !=\n[L61]       ROLE).\n[L62]    2. Context layer (MGM-only) — explicit contract: \"MGM line\n[L63]       is the only market reference; no other book, no consensus\n[L64]       line.\" Enforced by what the Framer delivers, affirmed in\n[L65]       prompt.\n[L66]    3. Prior layer (coin-flip) — explicit instruction: absent\n[L67]       evidence, each side of a prop is 50/50; the burden is on\n[L68]       evidence to move off the prior, and the analyst must\n[L69]       state what moved them. This is the anti-manufacture\n[L70]       mechanism.\n[L71]    4. Evidence layer (multi-factor) — fixed factor checklist\n[L72]       per bet type; analyst must address each factor as\n[L73]       SUPPORTS / OPPOSES / NO_DATA. NO_DATA must be free to\n[L74]       dominate.\n[L75]    5. Missing-data honesty layer — hard rule in prompt:\n[L76]       missing/stale data → state INSUFFICIENT_DATA as a\n[L77]       first-class verdict, never interpolate to neutral.\n[L78]       Mirrors the EC4 kill-switch lesson (France incident: 21%\n[L79]       data defaulted neutral).\n[L80]    6. Output layer (structured JSON) — fixed schema: verdict,\n[L81]       direction, confidence, factor_map, data_completeness_pct,\n[L82]       missing_fields[], rationale. Schema enforced at runtime\n[L83]       (see [F]); no free-text verdicts.\n\n[L85]    Anti-contamination rule: no analyst prompt contains another\n[L86]    analyst's output, the deterministic lane's output, or any\n[L87]    aggregate. Shared inputs only — never shared conclusions.\n\n[L89]    [C] CONVERGENCE SEMANTICS\n\n[L91]    What Convergence should compute (all deterministic,\n[L92]    auditable):\n\n[L94]    • Direction tally per pick: count of lane/panel leans\n[L95]      (OVER/UNDER/NO_PLAY).\n[L96]    • Agreement index — a descriptive measure (e.g., fraction of\n[L97]      non-abstain votes on the majority direction). Reported,\n[L98]      never used to boost.\n[L99]    • Dissent map — which lanes/personas dissent and their\n[L100]      stated factor. First-class output, not noise.\n[L101]    • Uncertainty aggregate — combined data-completeness; any\n[L102]      INSUFFICIENT_DATA from any lane propagates as a flag, not\n[L103]      a vote.\n\n[L105]    What Convergence should not do [DERIVED, flagged]:\n\n[L107]    • No confidence fusion into a single governing score. A\n[L108]      fused score that averages model confidences with\n[L109]      deterministic signals is Quant re-entry — it manufactures\n[L110]      precision and hides dissent. Flag: if a fused score is\n[L111]      retained, it must be display-only supporting evidence and\n[L112]      must never gate, rank, or veto. Ranking authority belongs\n[L113]      to Curator operating on\n[L114]      direction+agreement+data-sufficiency rules.\n[L115]    • No consensus bonus. Agreement on thin data is correlation,\n[L116]      not edge (existing EC4 law; carries over verbatim).\n[L117]    • No abstention erasure. Abstentions (NO_DATA, low\n[L118]      completeness) must shrink the eligible pool, not be\n[L119]      dropped from the denominator.\n\n[L121]    [D] CURATOR ROLE\n\n[L123]    Deterministic, non-model Curator is sufficient and correct\n[L124]    for the approved methodology: selection/filter/ranking by\n[L125]    declared rules over Convergence output is a mechanical\n[L126]    function, and correction #2 already bars it from reasoning.\n\n[L128]    Optional separate role (proposal, not silent expansion): a\n[L129]    Slate Reviewer [PROPOSED] — one model call, after Curator,\n[L130]    that sees the whole curated slate and answers only: \"is\n[L131]    there slate-level correlation risk?\" (e.g., three picks all\n[L132]    exposed to the same game/weather/pitcher). Justification:\n[L133]    per-pick independence is enforced everywhere, but cross-pick\n[L134]    correlation is invisible to every per-pick stage — no\n[L135]    existing stage has the whole slate as input. This is\n[L136]    methodologically valuable, cheap, and cleanly separable:\n[L137]    verdict SLATE_OK / SLATE_CORRELATION_FLAG, advisory to\n[L138]    Gatekeeper, no score mutation. If rejected, Curator alone\n[L139]    still passes — this is an enhancement, not a gap.\n\n[L141]    [E] KIMI GATEKEEPER CONTRACT\n\n[L143]    • Inputs: Curator output + Convergence provenance-tagged\n[L144]      record (including dissent map and uncertainty flags) +\n[L145]      data-completeness aggregate. Gatekeeper must see dissent;\n[L146]      a gatekeeper that sees only the surviving pick is\n[L147]      rubber-stamping.\n[L148]    • Authority: CONFIRM / CHALLENGE / FLAG / ESCALATE / KILL —\n[L149]      validation-only, confirmed. No score mutation, no pick\n[L150]      rewrite. Matches EC4 regression-guarded law.\n[L151]    • Verdict semantics: CHALLENGE and FLAG need defined\n[L152]      downstream meaning or they are dead verbs. Proposal:\n[L153]      CHALLENGE = returned to Convergence record as a dissonance\n[L154]      annotation (state changes, scores don't); FLAG = proceeds\n[L155]      with warning attached; both visible to Don.\n[L156]    • KILL conditions: stale/missing critical data, provenance\n[L157]      break (untagged or mixed-lane input), Curator rule\n[L158]      violation, MGM-line mismatch, any INSUFFICIENT_DATA on a\n[L159]      governing field.\n[L160]    • ESCALATE conditions: high agreement on low data\n[L161]      completeness (consensus-manufacture signature),\n[L162]      Gatekeeper's own confidence below threshold, internal\n[L163]      contradiction between direction tally and agreement index.\n[L164]    • BOOST: permanently removed — confirm. A validation-only\n[L165]      gatekeeper with BOOST is a contradiction in terms; any\n[L166]      promote-style helper is the exact EC4 regression the tests\n[L167]      guard against.\n[L168]    • Reasoning altering state without mutating scores: yes,\n[L169]      permitted and desirable — Gatekeeper reasoning may attach\n[L170]      annotations, force ESCALATE, or change recommendation\n[L171]      state (ACTIVE → CHALLENGED → KILLED). State transition ≠\n[L172]      score mutation. Keep that line bright.\n\n[L174]    [F] BEDROCK RUNTIME REALITY\n\n[L176]    Architecturally valid but operationally risky items:\n\n[L178]    1. Structured-output reliability — cross-family models\n[L179]       (Bedrock mix) have uneven JSON schema adherence.\n[L180]       Retry-on-parse-failure is mandatory; after N failures the\n[L181]       correct semantics is analyst abstention\n[L182]       (INSUFFICIENT_DATA-equivalent), not defaulting.\n[L183]       Partial-panel handling must be defined before runtime:\n[L184]       minimum quorum for Convergence to run (propose:\n[L185]       deterministic lane + ≥2 analysts; below quorum → whole\n[L186]       pick STOP, not degraded consensus).\n[L187]    2. Model-family diversity — genuine independence requires ≥2\n[L188]       model families on the panel; same-family personas are\n[L189]       correlated models wearing hats. But Bedrock family\n[L190]       availability is uneven per region/account — flag as\n[L191]       operational dependency.\n[L192]    3. Model substitution — must be a declared, versioned event.\n[L193]       Pin the brain: model version = dependency; a silent\n[L194]       Bedrock model update that shifts persona behavior must be\n[L195]       detectable via logged model IDs per call (provenance).\n[L196]    4. Timeout/retry — retries must be idempotent and logged; a\n[L197]       retried call that returns different reasoning than a\n[L198]       timed-out twin is fine (only one counts), but the log\n[L199]       must show which attempt was canonical.\n[L200]    5. Replayability — frozen dataset + logged prompts + logged\n[L201]       model IDs + logged raw responses = replayable. Without\n[L202]       raw-response logging, replayability is fiction. Require\n      it.\n[L204]    6. Terminal-first — realistic; no UI dependency before the\n[L205]       loop is proven. Agreed.\n\n[L207]    [G] STATE CLASSIFICATION\n\n[L209]    Gatekeeper verdict = deterministic state is incorrect as\n[L210]    stated [DERIVED]. Correct three-way split:\n\n[L212]    • Deterministic state: Framer output, Convergence tallies,\n[L213]      Curator selection — reproducible from inputs.\n[L214]    • Model-generated state: analyst verdicts, Gatekeeper\n[L215]      verdict (CONFIRM/CHALLENGE/…/KILL) — produced by a model\n[L216]      runtime, not reproducible bit-for-bit, even though the\n[L217]      verdict token set is constrained.\n[L218]    • Derived resolution state: the terminal recommendation\n[L219]      state (ACTIVE / CHALLENGED / FLAGGED / ESCALATED / KILLED\n[L220]      / STOP) — produced by deterministic resolution rules\n[L221]      applied to model verdicts. This is where determinism\n[L222]      legitimately re-enters.\n\n[L224]    Fix: \"Gatekeeper verdict is model-generated state; the\n[L225]    terminal pick state is a derived resolution state computed\n[L226]    deterministically from it.\" Small wording change,\n[L227]    load-bearing distinction — it's what keeps \"exactly one\n[L228]    terminal KILL\" and \"convergence is deterministic\" honest.\n[L229]    Belongs to architecture docs (Chiave), flagged by\n[L230]    methodology.\n\n[L232]    [H] EC3 → NEW SYSTEM DELTAS\n\n[L234]    • KEEP EC3: frozen estate as authoritative input;\n[L235]      independent lanes until single convergence; missing data =\n[L236]      explicit uncertainty, never neutral-default;\n[L237]      persona-differentiated analysts; quant as supporting\n[L238]      evidence; Don final authority.\n[L239]    • UPGRADE: Gatekeeper verbs expanded from EC3-style\n[L240]      confirm/kill to CONFIRM/CHALLENGE/FLAG/ESCALATE/KILL\n[L241]      (justified: dead middle-verbs in EC3 left no graded\n[L242]      response between pass and kill); Convergence output now\n[L243]      requires provenance tags + dissent map (EC3 convergence\n[L244]      was direction-only).\n[L245]    • REMOVE: BOOST / promote-style gatekeeper override (EC4\n[L246]      France-incident lesson); any fused governing score.\n[L247]    • NEW: MGM-only single-book constraint; explicit coin-flip\n[L248]      prior in prompt layer; Curator as hardened no-model stage;\n[L249]      derived-resolution state class; Bedrock multi-family panel\n[L250]      with quorum semantics.\n\n[L252]    [I] VERDICT\n\n[L254]    PASS WITH CHANGES — no topology redesign; all changes are\n[L255]    refinements within Chiave's architecture.\n\n[L257]    ┌───┬──────────────────────────────────┬───────────────────┐\n[L258]    │ # │ Change                           │ Belongs to        │\n[L259]    ├───┼──────────────────────────────────┼───────────────────┤\n[L260]    │ 1 │ Framer output provably free of   │ methodology       │\n[L261]    │   │ directional/derived fields       │ (rule) +          │\n[L262]    │   │                                  │ architecture  