el input contract (C3) — revised:\nField Class\tAllowed\tExamples\nSource facts\tYes\tRaw player stats, game logs, lineup status, injury designation, MGM line/odds\nFrame metadata\tYes\tMatchup ID, run ID, data_availability_flag, dataset timestamp\nDirectional/deterministic\tNo\tRolling averages with direction, hit-rate trends, form scores, lean indicators, any computed metric encoding \"over/under\" tendency\nRuntime enforcement: Analyst frame is validated against an explicit allowed-field schema before dispatch. Any field not in the allowed set → frame rejected, error logged, analyst invocation aborted for that matchup. This is a hard gate, not a warning.\nRationale: If BINDER_FRAMER encodes directional conclusions, analyst independence is violated by injection — analysts would anchor on pre-computed direction rather than reasoning from raw evidence. The previous correction blocked deterministic lane outputs from reaching analysts; this correction blocks the same contamination at the framer level, where it is more insidious because it looks like \"helpful framing.\"\nC2 Addition: Provenance Survival Invariant\nNew architectural invariant: Provenance origin labels survive the convergence boundary and remain intact through all downstream stages.\nLabel taxonomy:\nLabel\tMeaning\nDET\tOriginated from Deterministic Lane\nPANEL:<persona>\tOriginated from a specific analyst persona (e.g., PANEL:blind, PANEL:contrarian)\nCURATOR\tOriginated from Curator selection logic\nGATEKEEPER\tOriginated from Kimi gatekeeper verdict\nPropagation rules:\nAt Convergence: Every output field is tagged with its origin label(s). Direction tally → DET + PANEL:*. Agreement index → computed from PANEL:* set. Dissent map → each dissent entry attributed to PANEL:<persona>. Uncertainty flag → attributed to its source (data gap = DET, analyst disagreement = PANEL:*).\nAt Curator: Curator may attach CURATOR labels to inclusion/exclusion decisions. Original labels on convergence outputs pass through unchanged.\nAt Gatekeeper: Gatekeeper verdict is tagged GATEKEEPER. All upstream labels on the pick being evaluated remain attached and readable.\nAt Terminal: Full provenance chain preserved in terminal artifact. Every pick traces to its DET and PANEL:* origins with no flattening.\nProhibited: No stage may:\nStrip origin labels from evidence\nFlatten attributed dissent into anonymous \"majority vs minority\"\nReplace PANEL:<persona> labels with generic PANEL or AI\nMerge DET + PANEL:* into an undifferentiated CONVERGENCE label\nArtifact impact: convergence_result.json, curated_slate.json, gatekeeper_verdict.json, and terminal_artifact.json all carry a provenance field on every decision-relevant element.\nC3 Correction: State Classification\nRevised state model:\nStage\tState Class\tRationale\nFrozen dataset\tImmutable\tSource of record, hash-verified\nBINDER_FRAMER output\tDeterministic\tSource facts only, no inference\nDeterministic lane\tDeterministic\tComputed from source facts, no model involvement\nAnalyst responses\tModel-generated\tEach analyst's independent reasoning via Bedrock\nConvergence result\tDeterministic\tDeterministic join of deterministic + model-generated inputs; computation is deterministic even though inputs include model outputs\nCurator selection\tDeterministic\tRule-based filter/rank on convergence output, no model\nGatekeeper verdict\tModel-generated\tCorrected. Kimi is a model invocation. Verdict is model-generated, not deterministic.\nTerminal resolution\tDerived resolution\tDeterministically resolved from gatekeeper verdict + pipeline state. Produces terminal state: ACTIVE / CHALLENGED / FLAGGED / ESCALATED / KILLED / STOP\nDon decision\tHuman-decision\tOutside pipeline\nKey correction: Gatekeeper verdict was previously classified as deterministic validation. It is model-generated. Kimi reasons about the slate and issues a verdict — that reasoning is a model output, even though the verdict space is constrained to five values.\nDerived resolution state is a new class. It is deterministic in the sense that the mapping from (gatekeeper verdict, pipeline state) → terminal state is a fixed function, but it is \"derived resolution\" not \"deterministic\" because it consumes model-generated input (the gatekeeper verdict) and produces the terminal resolution that Don acts on.\nKILL authority chain (reaffirmed):\nKimi Gatekeeper (model-generated) → issues KILL verdict\n         ↓\n    Terminal (derived resolution) → resolves KILLED state\n         ↓\n    Don (human) → sees KILLED, cannot reverse\nNo other component issues KILL. Terminal resolves; it does not judge. Don sees; he does not override KILL.\nB UPDATED INVARIANTS\nSource-only framing. BINDER_FRAMER outputs source facts only. No directional, derived, or deterministic-lane content reaches the Analyst Panel.\nAnalyst independence. Analyst Panel receives source-only frames. No deterministic lane outputs. No other analyst outputs. No cross-analyst communication.\nSingle convergence. Exactly one CONVERGENCE component. Deterministic lane + analyst panel join at one point. No second pass.\nNo governing fused score. Convergence produces descriptive outputs: direction tally, agreement index, dissent map, uncertainty/data-sufficiency state. Any numeric fusion is display-only — may not rank, gate, promote, veto, or drive selection.\nProvenance survival. Origin labels (DET, PANEL:<persona>, CURATOR, GATEKEEPER) survive convergence and remain intact through Curator → Gatekeeper → Terminal. No flattening.\nGatekeeper is model-generated, validation-only. Kimi verdict is model-generated state, constrained to five values, and may not mutate scores or picks. KILL is final.\nSingular KILL authority. Only Kimi Gatekeeper issues KILL. Terminal resolves it. No reversal downstream.\nPanel quorum. DETERMINISTIC_LANE + ≥2 valid independent analysts. Below quorum → STOP.\nINSUFFICIENT_DATA is abstention. Not a directional vote. Not neutral. Not zero.\nFrozen dataset authority. No data reacquisition. No live API calls outside Bedrock model invocations.\nMGM-only market reference. No other sportsbook lines enter the pipeline.\nMODEL != ROLE != SEAT. Role-occupant mapping in config. Model substitution does not change role semantics.\nTerminal-first execution. CLI + artifacts + structured logs. No UI dependency.\nC TOPOLOGY CHECK\nUNCHANGED\nTopology remains:\nFraming ──┬──→ Deterministic Lane ──┐\n           │                        │\n           └──→ Analyst Panel ─────┘──→ Convergence → Curator → Gatekeeper → Terminal → Don\nNo components added, removed, or reordered. Corrections are boundary tightenings (C1), attribute additions (C2), and classification corrections (C3) — none alter the graph.\nD ARCHITECTURE VERDICT\nPASS\nAll three corrections are applied. Architecture is coherent, methodology-faithful, and bounded. No outstanding changes required.\nE RAGNO READINESS\nREADY\nThe architecture now has:\nUnambiguous component boundaries with prohibited responsibilities\nSource-only framing with runtime enforcement gate\nProvenance survival invariant with explicit label taxonomy\nCorrected state classification (gatekeeper = model-generated)\nSingular KILL authority chain\nPanel quorum rule\nAll eight existing boundaries verified intact\nNo pending corrections\nSufficient for Principal Consultant reconciliation.\nSTATUS:            PASS\nCONFIDENCE:        95%\nCHANGES APPLIED:   3 bounded corrections — no topology change\nNEXT ROUTE:        Don/Coda → Ragno/K3 Swarm", "text_chars": 8121, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": ["convergence_result.json", "curated_slate.json", "gatekeeper_verdict.json", "terminal_artifact.json"], "model_slug": null, "has_voice_metadata": false, "empty_text_parts": 0, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "df526d1f-70ae-4309-9611-bf42e907c6a0", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1789688866.500555, "updated_at": 1789688894.129094, "status": "finis