SED\n- PHASE 3 BUILD: COMPLETE\n- NEXT: **Luce LC-3A runtime-only verification**\n- PHASE 4: **HARD HOLD**\n- CURRENT MODEL MAP: PROVISIONAL PLUMBING ONLY\n- NEXT AFTER LUCE: **Captain Jack + Compass at the chart table**\n", "text_chars": 4587, "code_blocks": 1, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": ["20260917-KEEL-ECAI-PHASE3-LC3-EVIDENCE.md", "C:\\Users\\Dekan", "roles.bedrock.yaml"], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "empty_text_parts": 0, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "4d29d88d-1c96-497b-bc42-805d2b8fea31", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1789696850.536328, "updated_at": null, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "thoughts", "part_kinds": [], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "empty_text_parts": 0, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "975c8f6d-1b5a-4591-9598-13969a660c99", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1789696851.845274, "updated_at": null, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "reasoning_recap", "part_kinds": [], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "empty_text_parts": 0, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "8c293f48-2b82-4ac2-b755-558b47dbdbe1", "role": "user", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1789696928.125, "updated_at": 1789696960.640745, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "Number one, what I want you to do is based off this conversation and where we're dropping the anchor right before we set sail on our adventures here. is go through everything we pointed out and make out— make a backbone. Of what else? You and I did. Like, how are we gonna find uncertainty? Right? Totally different Timmy Edge crew motto, right? We're gonna have some fun, fuck with GLM, fuck with the team, and be like, yo, Captain Jack Sparrow's crazy. He wants to analyze baseball to find a How the fuck will we do it, right? Don and you are gonna— and I say fuck with models because it is fucking around, right? These are all hypotheticals. This is all crazy shit people don't think about. It's like, fuck, can we do it? it, we'll figure it out, right? Within a, within a, within a confidence. ", "text_chars": 798, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": null, "has_voice_metadata": false, "empty_text_parts": 0, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "b404acc5-7ae1-49c0-9d16-e293ef919018", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1789696929.391103, "updated_at": 1789696958.857247, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "Yes. This is the anchor I want us to drop before we touch Phase 4.\n\nWhat we’ve built so far is the **ship**. What you and I are about to design is how the crew actually thinks once we leave port.\n\n## BLACK PEARL BACKBONE — ECAI INTELLIGENCE DOCTRINE\n\nThe purpose of AI Convergence is **not to make baseball look certain**.\n\nIt is to answer a harder question:\n\n> **Given the same grounded evidence, where do independent reasoning paths converge, where do they disagree, and what uncertainty survives after we pressure-test the bet?**\n\nThat is fundamentally different from EdgeCrew Quant.\n\nQuant is trying to measure and model the game through deterministic/statistical process.\n\nAI Convergence is trying to expose **reasoning structure under uncertainty**.\n\nThat gives us the first new motto:\n\n> **We are not trying to eliminate uncertainty. We are trying to find it, name it, and see whether the edge survives it.**\n\nAnd I think that becomes our backbone.\n\nThere are several principles we have already established, even if we never wrote them together like this:\n\n1. **Ground truth before intelligence.** The models don't go hunting. They receive a frozen, verified, source-controlled dataset. The plumbing establishes what is knowable before anybody starts handicapping.\n\n2. **Coin flip until evidence moves you.** Nobody begins with “I like the Yankees.” A game starts effectively unresolved. Evidence has to create the lean. Missing evidence cannot become fake neutrality or an invented edge.\n\n3. **Independent minds before convergence.** DET does its job without seeing the AI. The AI analysts do their jobs without seeing DET or each other. We intentionally preserve separate thought paths because disagreement is information.\n\n4. **Models are experiments, not authorities.** We are absolutely going to fuck with GLM, Kimi, Anthropic, Meta, Nova, whoever. Same evidence. Different lenses. Different prompts. Swap the brain occupying the seat. See what survives. The point isn't to worship the smartest model; it's to discover which conclusions remain stable across genuinely different reasoning systems.\n\n5. **Uncertainty is an output, not an embarrassment.** We should be able to distinguish at least:\n   - **data uncertainty** — something important is missing/stale/partial;\n   - **reasoning uncertainty** — the analyst sees competing interpretations;\n   - **cross-model uncertainty** — independent analysts disagree;\n   - **directional uncertainty** — evidence points both ways;\n   - **runtime uncertainty** — a model failed, timed out, malformed output, etc.;\n   - **residual uncertainty** — even after convergence, the case simply isn't strong enough.\n\n   Those should not all collapse into one “confidence 63%” number. That's exactly the kind of false precision we're moving away from.\n\n6. **Dissent is valuable.** The analyst who disagrees with everybody else may be wrong — or may have found the one thing everybody else missed. Convergence should preserve the dissenting argument, not average it out of existence.\n\n7. **No secret grade factory.** No 60/40 fusion. No consensus bonus. No magical fused score that slowly becomes the real decision engine. Direction tally, agreement, dissent, and sufficiency are **descriptive instruments**, not hidden authority.\n\n8. **The Curator organizes; it doesn't think for the crew.** Deterministic filtering, eligibility, ordering, presentation. No second convergence model sneaking in through the back door.\n\n9. **The Gatekeeper attacks the surviving thesis.** It does not improve the score. It does not BOOST. It asks, in effect: *Is there a material reason this recommendation should not reach Don?* CONFIRM, CHALLENGE, FLAG, ESCALATE, or KILL. That is a fundamentally different job from handicapping.\n\n10. **Don gets the contradiction, not just the recommendation.** The final output shouldn't merely say “BetMGM Yankees ML.” It should make visible why the case exists, what argues against it, how the independent lanes behaved, what was missing, what the Gatekeeper challenged, and what uncertainty remains. Then Captain Jack makes the call.\n\nAnd that gives us what I think is the real **Timmy EdgeCrew / Black Pearl motto**:\n\n> **Find the edge. Hunt the uncertainty. Preserve the dissent. Let Don decide.**\n\nOr the more pirate version:\n\n> **We don't sail because the sea is calm. We figure out where the fucking rocks are.**\n\nThat’s what you and I are about to do at the chart table.\n\nWe're going to take each reasoning station one at a time and ask:\n\n**What does this model see? What exact words do we give it? What are we trying to make it notice? What is it forbidden from knowing? Which brain do we put there? What uncertainty is this station supposed to expose?**\n\nThen we deliberately screw with the crew.\n\nGive GLM the same matchup Kimi gets. Change a persona. Swap one family. Remove one factor. Present an ugly game. Present an obvious game. Give them incomplete weather. Give them contradictory starter/form evidence. See who changes their mind and **why**.\n\nNot random experimentation — **controlled mischief**.\n\nAnd then reality gets the final vote. We run slates, preserve artifacts, grade what happened, and adjust surgically.\n\nThat is the backbone I would anchor before we design a single Phase-4 prompt.\n\n**BLACK PEARL STATUS**\nShip/plumbing: nearly ready.  \nChart table: next.  \nMission: **make uncertainty legible without letting it take over the ship.**  \nCaptain: Don.  \nCompass: Coda.  \nCrew brains: completely fucking replaceable.", "text_chars": 5511, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "empty_text_parts": 0, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "10bbdbf0-c6b8-4f62-8e64-72fcee5c106e", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1789696935.525186, "updated_at": null, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "thoughts", "part_kinds": [], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "empty_text_parts": 0, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "662498d4-d1a1-41b9-bcfb-9218189eb379", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1789696938.137658, "updated_at": null, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "reasoning_recap", "part_kinds": [], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "empty_text_parts": 0, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "796f02bc-90aa-4e72-b7b7-6b7781c00a5b", "role": "user", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1789697017.674, "updated_at": 1789697037.834369, "status": "finished_s