ensure manifest changes are actually diffed and recorded. The primitive exists; orchestration must use it.\n2. `KeyboardInterrupt` being swallowed into `ModelInvocationError` is a minor runtime robustness issue for later. Not something we touch while designing Phase 4.\n\nAnd Luce was explicit about the thing that matters most:\n\n> current analyst/gatekeeper model assignments are **plumbing config only**, not Don-approved intelligence architecture.\n\nGood. That means nothing has gotten ahead of us.\n\n## ANCHOR DROPPED\n\nWe now have the ship through:\n\n**Frozen data → Binding → Framing → DET → Runtime Core**\n\nEverything after that is now **Captain Jack + Compass territory**.\n\nPhase 4 does **not** start until you and I decide:\n\n- how many analyst lanes exist\n- what each lane is trying to detect\n- exact persona/lens for each\n- exact prompt wording\n- exact evidence each lane sees\n- exact output schema semantics\n- which model family occupies each lane\n- whether one family can occupy multiple lanes\n- how we want disagreement expressed\n- what counts as uncertainty\n- what the Gatekeeper sees\n- exact Gatekeeper wording\n- what the Curator ranks on\n- which parts are fixed doctrine vs experimental config\n- cost/latency tradeoffs\n- substitution rules for live operation\n\nThis is no longer a plumbing discussion.\n\nThis is the **intelligence architecture**.\n\nAnd I think the right next move is not another seat prompt. It’s you and me at the chart table building the Phase-4 map from scratch, using the backbone we just anchored:\n\n> **Find the edge. Hunt the uncertainty. Preserve the dissent. Let Don decide.**\n\n**SESSION FOOTER**\n- PHASE 1: CLOSED\n- PHASE 2: CLOSED\n- PHASE 3: CLOSED\n- TESTS: **128 PASS**\n- PHASE 4: **HOLD**\n- CURRENT MODEL MAP: provisional only\n- NEXT: **DON + CODA — ECAI INTELLIGENCE ARCHITECTURE**\n- CAPTAIN JACK STATUS: **AT THE CHART TABLE**", "text_chars": 2974, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_referen