ype": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "Yes. **Anchor drop means we freeze the ship before we start changing the intelligence layer.**\n\nAt this point I would not trust “we can reconstruct it later.” We have too many decisions, corrections, artifacts, and verified gates. We want one **reproducible pre-Phase-4 checkpoint** that we can restore if we screw around with prompts/models and hate the result.\n\nThe backbone should be:\n\n**1. Git checkpoint of the build repo**\n`C:\\Users\\Dekan AI Brother\\GCE_DON\\GCE_EC8\\GCE_EC8_Build\\`\n\nCommit everything currently accepted through Phase 3, including:\n- `ecai\\`\n- `config\\`\n- `tests\\`\n- `ECAI_IMPLEMENTATION_CHOICES.md`\n- current schemas/runtime code\n- all tests at **128 passing**\n\nTag it something like:\n\n`ECAI_PRE_PHASE4_ANCHOR_2026-09-17`\n\nThat becomes the code restore point.\n\n**2. Preserve the governing design/spec artifacts**\nAt minimum:\n- P20 Calibro Implementation Design **Rev 3**\n- P21 Ragno review\n- P22 corrections\n- P23 release check\n- Talon build-operation brief\n- LC-1 / LC-2 / LC-3A Luce findings/evidence\n- Keel Phase 1 / 2 / 3 evidence handoffs\n- our current Black Pearl / uncertainty doctrine as a new anchor note\n\nThis is the **why and what**, not just the code.\n\n**3. Preserve the exact frozen-data reference**\nDo not necessarily duplicate the entire MLB data estate into the repo, but record:\n- exact frozen dataset path\n- dataset identity\n- freeze timestamp\n- composite digest\n- 49-entry manifest state\n- 12 eligible / 3 excluded\n- provenance references\n\nThat makes the code checkpoint reproducible against the dataset we actually used.\n\n**4. Create one immutable anchor bundle**\nSomething like:\n\n`ECAI_ANCHOR_PRE_PHASE4_2026-09-17\\`\n\ncontaining:\n- `README_ANCHOR.md`\n- `BUILD_STATE.md`\n- `METHODOLOGY_AND_GOVERNANCE.md`\n- `ARTIFACT_MANIFEST.txt`\n- `GIT_STATE.txt`\n- `DATASET_BINDING.md`\n- copies of the authoritative P20/P21/P22/P23/Talon/Luce/Keel handoffs\n- optional ZIP of the build tree\n\nThen hash the bundle.\n\n**5. Back it up off-machine**\nTwo destinations is enough:\n\n- **Google Drive**: durable human-readable anchor bundle\n- **Private GitHub repo**: code + history + tags\n\nDo **not** push:\n- `.secrets`\n- tokens\n- AWS credentials\n- local auth/session stores\n- raw private runtime credentials\n\nI would use Google Drive for the **full governance/handoff/archive bundle** and GitHub for the **code/config/tests**.\n\nAnd I’d make Talon coordinate it, Keel do the Git mechanics, and Luce verify the final checkpoint.\n\nUse this:\n\n```text\n[ANCHOR-DROP-1] TALON — ECAI PRE-PHASE4 FREEZE + BACKUP\n\nObjective:\nCreate a recoverable, verified checkpoint of the entire accepted ECAI state BEFORE Don/Coda begin Phase-4 intelligence/prompt/model experimentation.\n\nThis is a preservation operation, not a redesign.\n\nCURRENT RELEASE STATE:\n- Phase 1 CLOSED\n- Phase 2 CLOSED\n- Phase 3 CLOSED\n- LC-3A PASS\n- tests = 128 passing\n- Phase 4 = DON/CODA HOLD\n- P20 current = Rev 3\n- Chiave CLOSED\n- Corrado CLOSED\n\n1. KEEL — GIT CHECKPOINT\n\nBuild root:\nC:\\Users\\Dekan AI Brother\\GCE_DON\\GCE_EC8\\GCE_EC8_Build\\\n\nVerify working tree.\n\nExclude all secrets/auth/session material.\n\nCommit the accepted current state.\n\nCreate tag:\n\nECAI_PRE_PHASE4_ANCHOR_2026-09-17\n\nRecord:\n- commit SHA\n- tag\n- git status\n- test result\n- Python/runtime versions\n\nRun:\npython -m pytest tests -q\n\nExpected:\n128 passed.\n\n2. ANCHOR ARTIFACT BUNDLE\n\nCreate:\n\nC:\\Users\\Dekan AI Brother\\GCE_DON\\GCE_EC8\\\nECAI_ANCHOR_PRE_PHASE4_2026-09-17\\\n\nInclude copies or authoritative references for:\n\n- P20 Calibro implementation design Rev 3\n- P21 Ragno fidelity review\n- P22 bounded corrections\n- P23 Ragno release\n- Talon ECAI build-operation brief\n- Keel Phase 1 evidence\n- Luce LC-1 findings/recheck\n- Keel Phase 2 evidence\n- Luce LC-2 result\n- Keel Phase 3 evidence\n- Luce LC-3A result\n- ECAI_IMPLEMENT