una S 2.1 (free)\n- Inkling (free)\n- Laguna XS 2.1 (free)\n- Gemini Omni Flash Preview\n- North Mini Code (free)\n- GLM 5.2 (free)\n- Nemotron 3 Ultra (free)\n- Nemotron 3.5 Content Safety (free)\n- Nemotron 3 Nano Omni (free)\n- Gemma 4 26B A4B (free)\n- Gemma 4 31B (free)\n- Nemotron 3 Super (free)\n\n**Google**\n- Gemini 3.1 Flash TTS Preview\n- Gemini 3.1 Flash Live Preview\n- Gemini 3.1 Flash Lite Preview\n\nOne small note: I’m transcribing exactly what’s visible in the screenshots, so this is a **screen-captured inventory**, not yet a verified capability/model-family map.\n\nFor Luce, I’d have him truth this next: **exact model identity, provider, family, whether the “free” tier is actually callable, context window, reasoning/code bias, and whether any names are aliases/wrappers rather than distinct base models.**", "text_chars": 1386, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "empty_text_parts": 0, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "0bf47525-df12-480b-9ec5-3fa7f8bed765", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1789719302.106776, "updated_at": null, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "reasoning_recap", "part_kinds": [], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "empty_text_parts": 0, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "cc519b79-fc54-4698-9876-9e3739409584", "role": "user", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1789719514.371, "updated_at": 1789719557.878189, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "Yeah, I'm already doing that. All right, I'm doing that in my shorthand. Good job, by the way. All right, now you and I are gonna have some fun because I wanna have some fun. Basically. He's putting it together in my own words, exactly what you said, but also a little paragraph of what it's good at. He has no context of what we're doing. I want you to do the same. But for our crew. And again, You're not the one fucking pushing these prompts. You're not doing anything. You're the framework. So in your mind, let's build that and you and I will rank them. You and I are going to have some fun and pick, pick who the horses are. And then I'll run the prompts and we'll map the results. And we'll figure out what's good with what. As it relates to the Edge Crew pirate ship Captain Jack. Crazy model process we got going on. ", "text_chars": 826, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": null, "has_voice_metadata": false, "empty_text_parts": 0, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "9fd694ee-f2a5-4fec-969f-9b9c39f8b210", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1789719518.331924, "updated_at": 1789719557.562625, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "Yep. Now we get to have some fun.\n\nI’d build this as a **Captain Jack draft board**, not a benchmark leaderboard. We are not asking, “What is the smartest model?” We’re asking:\n\n> **Which weird bastard might bring a useful, independent reasoning style to the Black Pearl?**\n\nAnd these are **our provisional scouting grades**, before Luce comes back with the verified model cards and before any of them see Trial 01.\n\n| Draft slot | Model | Black Pearl scouting hypothesis | Pirate job I’d audition it for |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| **1** | **GLM 5.2** | My first horse. Likely strong at structured reasoning, connecting factors, and following a bounded analytical job without needing us to over-script it. More interesting because GLM already appeared historically in EC4, but we can give it a completely different Black Pearl job. | **First Mate / heavyweight inference** |\n| **2** | **DeepSeek V4 Flash 0731** | Strong candidate for finding relationships and attacking a thesis quickly. I’d specifically test whether it sees causal chains instead of merely summarizing the supplied numbers. | **Raider / counter-thesis hunter** |\n| **3** | **Qwen3.8 27B** | Very interesting because it gives us another model family that should reason differently from GLM/Kimi. I want to know whether it is disciplined under sparse evidence or starts filling holes. | **Navigator / independent read** |\n| **4** | **Nemotron 3 Super** | This is the Nemotron I’d test first. Potentially useful as a careful critic or structured reviewer. I’m particularly interested in whether it handles “I don’t know” better than models that want to answer everything. | **Ship inspector / uncertainty hunter** |\n| **5** | **MiMo V2.5** | Wild card with enough apparent scale to be worth testing. This is exactly the type of model Black Pearl exists for: we don’t know what peculiar reasoning capability it might surface until we give it the same game as everybody else. | **Mystery mercenary** |\n| **6** | **Nemotron 3 Ultra** | Second Nemotron horse. I would not run every Nemotron variant immediately because that destroys family independence, but Ultra deserves a head-to-head with Super later. | **Reserve inspector / challenger** |\n| **7** | **Gemini Omni Flash Preview** | Could be a useful fast synthesizer, but I’d be careful because “Omni/Flash” may emphasize breadth/speed rather than deep sports inference. Still absolutely worth an audition. | **Lookout / broad pattern scan** |\n| **8** | **Nex-N2.5-Pro** | Unknown enough to be interesting. “Pro” gets it into the audition pool, but Luce needs to tell us what it actually is before we assign any theoretical specialty. | **Unknown deckhand — prove yourself** |\n| **9** | **Ling 3.0 Flash Fin** | “Fin” makes this particularly interesting for a betting/market environment, but I’m not going to assume that means financial reasoning until Luce verifies it. If it does, it could become a great price/market skeptic. | **Purser / market skeptic** |\n| **10** | **Muse Spark 1.3** | I would test this precisely because I know less about it. If everybody else reaches the obvious conclusion and Muse produces a coherent alien angle, that may be valuable. | **Crazy guy in the crow’s nest** |\n| **11** | **Nemotron 3.5 Lightning** | Likely speed-oriented. Worth testing as a cheap first-pass reader, but I would not expect it to beat Super/Ultra at our deeper reasoning trial until it proves otherwise. | **Fast scout** |\n| **12** | **Ling 3.0 Flash Sante** | Name suggests another specialization, but we need Luce’s identity card before assigning it anything. Definitely not tossing it overboard yet. | **Unknown specialist** |\n| **13** | **Ling 3.0 Flash VL** | “VL” may indicate a vision-language orientation, which would not give us much in Trial 01’s JSON/text environment unless it has strong general reasoning too. | **Map reader / later multimodal trial** |\n| **14** | **Dots3-Note Preview** | Could be good at extraction/organization rather than original inference. Might actually become useful downstream for turning messy analyst outputs into structured artifacts. | **Ship’s clerk** |\n| **15** | **Inkling / Inkling Small** | Unknown. “Small” probably isn’t where I start for the heavyweight analysis, but cheap/small models can sometimes be surprisingly good at constrained classification. | **Cabin boy trial** |\n| **16** | **Laguna S 2.1 / Laguna XS 2.1** | Same story: unknown until verified. XS sounds especially likely to be optimized for efficiency rather than deep synthesis. | **Deckhands** |\n| **17** | **Nex-N2.5-Mini** | I’d test only after Pro. Could be useful later for cheap filtering if it tracks the stronger model surprisingly well. | **Junior lookout** |\n| **18** | **Muse Spark 1.2** | We already have 1.3. Unless there is some unusual difference, I’d start with the newer sibling and leave 1.2 on the dock. | **Reserve crew** |\n| **19** | **LFM2.5-2.6B** | At 2.6B by name, this sounds much smaller than what I want for open-ended inference. Could still be useful later for deterministic-ish routing/classification. | **Messenger, not navigator** |\n| **20** | **Nemotron 3 Nano Omni** | Same concept: potentially great for cheap classification/routing, but I would not waste our first serious baseball trial evaluating it as a heavyweight analyst. | **Runner / message carrier** |\n| **21** | **North Mini Code** | Sounds coding-oriented. Wrong audition for Trial 01. Could be useful elsewhere on the ship. | **Shipwright apprentice** |\n| **22** | **Gemma 4 26B A4B / Gemma 4 31B** | Worth eventual testing, but I’d put them behind the more intriguing inference candidates initially. Could surprise us. | **Reserve analytical crew** |\n| **23** | **Nemotron 3.5 Content Safety** | Not an analyst candidate. Its specialization sounds wrong for the job. Could potentially be useful for other validation functions, but not baseball inference. | **Harbor master — stays ashore** |\n| **24** | **Gemini Flash TTS / Live / Lite previews** | These sound optimized around modality/live/efficiency rather than our specific text reasoning trial. Not where Captain Jack spends tonight’s ammunition. | **Different ship entirely** |\n\n### My first race\n\nIf we’re **not spending all fucking night**, I would put six horses in the gate:\n\n**GLM 5.2  \nDeepSeek V4 Flash  \nQwen3.8 27B  \nNemotron 3 Super  \nMiMo V2.5  \none wild-card unknown — probably Muse Spark 1.3 or Nex-N2.5-Pro**\n\nThat gives us multiple families and, more importantly, models that are plausibly different enough that we may actually learn something.\n\nThen I would deliberately **not run Kimi** in Trial 01.\n\nKimi is our known quantity. We already know Kimi can play baseball in our environment. Black Pearl’s purpose tonight is to find the weird bastard who says:\n\n> “Captain, everybody is staring at the starter. I think the