n edge exists.\nDo not assume favorites are good bets.\nDo not assume underdogs are value.\nDo not treat ERA alone as sufficient evidence.\n\nPASS is valid.\n\n==================================================\n3. ANALYTICAL MISSION\n==================================================\n\nReview the entire slate.\n\nChoose NO MORE THAN FIVE games that most deserve further investigation.\n\nFor each selected game return:\n\nGAME:\nINITIAL READ:\nWHY IT CAUGHT MY ATTENTION:\nPOTENTIAL THESIS:\nSTRONGEST COUNTER-THESIS:\nBIGGEST UNKNOWN:\nWHAT I WOULD WANT NEXT:\nCLASSIFICATION:\nINTEREST | WATCH | NEEDS DATA | PASS\n\nThen return:\n\nTOP 3 MOST INTERESTING GAMES:\n1.\n2.\n3.\n\nMOST IMPORTANT UNKNOWN ACROSS THE SLATE:\n\nONE THING I NOTICED THAT ANOTHER ANALYST MAY MISS:\n\n==================================================\n4. OUTPUT CAPTURE\n==================================================\n\nCreate a filesystem-safe MODEL_SLUG from your actual model/runtime identity.\n\nWrite your complete response as UTF-8 Markdown to:\n\nC:\\Users\\Dekan AI Brother\\Desktop\\Black Pearl EC\\OpenCode Free Test Run\\\nBP_T01_<MODEL_SLUG>_2026-09-18.md\n\nIf that filename already exists, append:\n_02, _03, etc.\n\nDo not overwrite another analyst's artifact.\n\nThe file must begin with:\n\n# BLACK PEARL PROVING GROUNDS — TRIAL 01\n\nMODEL / RUNTIME:\nPROVIDER:\nVERSION / MODEL ID:\nROLE: Independent Blind Analyst\nRUN TIMESTAMP:\nTRIAL ID: BP-T01\nSOURCE DATASET: BLACK_PEARL_TRIAL01_SPARSE_SLATE_2026-09-18.json\nANALYSIS MODE: BLIND\nOUTCOME DATA ACCESSED: NO\nOTHER ANALYST OUTPUT ACCESSED: NO\n\nThen include the complete analysis exactly as produced.\n\nAt the end include:\n\n## SELF-IDENTIFICATION / PROVENANCE\n\nI certify that this analysis was produced independently from the supplied\nevidence package and that I did not read another analyst's output before\ncompleting this run.\n\nMODEL / RUNTIME:\nTIMESTAMP:\nOUTPUT FILE:\n\n==================================================\n