“I don’t have enough evidence”\n\nis beating a smarter model that says:\n\n> “I bet the missing starter is probably an ace.”\n\nFor this Black Pearl lane, that matters a lot.\n\nSecond big lesson: **we need to separate creative inference from grounded analysis**.\n\nNemotron Ultra and MiMo are not necessarily bad models. They may be excellent on the later crazy ship where inference is explicitly allowed. But in this sparse blind trial, they keep promoting memory/speculation into evidence.\n\nThat is a berth mismatch, not necessarily a brain-quality failure.\n\nThird lesson: there are already clear role archetypes emerging:\n\n- **Dots3** = anomaly hunter\n- **Muse 1.3** = disciplined pattern analyst\n- **Nex Mini** = skeptic / uncertainty cop\n- **Nemotron Ultra** = speculative scout\n- **Ling** = market-curious analyst with sloppy self-audit\n- **MiMo** = creative generalist with weak boundaries\n\nThat’s fucking useful.\n\n### The race right now\n\nIf Captain Jack had to pick the current top tier before the big boys finish, I’d say:\n\n**Muse Spark 1.3  \nDots3-Note Preview  \nNex-N2.5-Mini**\n\nThose three have shown the most distinct and useful Black Pearl behavior so far.\n\nThen behind them:\n\n**Muse 1.2  \nLing Fin  \nLing VL**\n\nSpecialist bucket:\n\n**Nemotron Ultra  \nMiMo**\n\nCut:\n\n**LFM**\n\nAnd now the good part: the next wave is stronger.\n\nPending:\n- **Nemotron 3.5 Lightning Free** — still grinding\n- **Nex-N2.5-Pro** — very interesting because Mini already surprised us\n- **DeepSeek V4 Flash 0731**\n- **one other current runner** you’ve got going that I’ll identify from the artifact when it lands\n\nThe single model I’m most curious about now is actually **Nex Pro**.\n\nBecause if the Mini already has strong restraint and the Pro keeps that discipline while improving arithmetic/reasoning depth, we may have accidentally found a serious horse in the fog.\n\nAnd DeepSeek is the opposite test: known workhorse, much higher market presence, so now w