nsive lineup strength.\n\n[L98] **WHAT I WOULD WANT NEXT:**\n[L99] Globe Life Field park factor for runs, Blue Jays offensive lineup strength vs righties, Rangers bullpen performance.\n\n[L101] **CLASSIFICATION:**\n[L102] INTEREST\n\n---\n[L105] ### GAME 4: Chicago Cubs@Cincinnati Reds 2026-09-18\n\n[L107] **INITIAL READ:**\n[L108] - Away: Clay Holmes (R) - ERA 2.85, WHIP 1.15, K9 6.97\n[L109] - Home: Chase Burns (R) - ERA 2.80, WHIP 1.15, K9 10.76\n[L110] - Moneyline: Cubs -135, Reds +110\n[L111] - Run Line: Cubs -1.5 (+125), Reds +1.5 (-155)\n[L112] - Total: 8.5\n\n[L114] **WHY IT CAUGHT MY ATTENTION:**\n[L115] Burns has exceptional K9 (10.76) compared to Holmes (6.97) - a 3.79 K9 differential. WHIPs and ERAs are nearly identical. Reds are +110 underdogs despite Chase Burns having substantially higher strikeout upside. The moneyline might not fully reflect Burns' edge.\n\n[L117] **POTENTIAL THESIS:**\n[L118] Reds moneyline +110 offers value. Burns' K9 differential suggests he will generate more outs via strikeouts than Holmes, potentially neutralizing home field advantage despite Cubs being favored.\n\n[L120] **STRONGEST COUNTER-THESIS:**\n[L121] Home field at Great American Ball Park, and Holmes' 2.85 ERA vs Burns' 2.80 ERA are nearly identical. Small ERA gap slightly favors Cubs. Vegas correctly prices Cubs as slight favorites.\n\n[L123] **BIGGEST UNKNOWN:**\n[L124] Great American Ball Park run environment, recent team form.\n\n[L126] **WHAT I WOULD WANT NEXT:**\n[L127] Recent team offensive stats at home vs away, bullpen performance trends, splits vs LHB/RHP.\n\n[L129] **CLASSIFICATION:**\nWATCH\n\n---\n[L133] ### GAME 5: New York Yankees@Arizona Diamondbacks 2026-09-18\n\n[L135] **INITIAL READ:**\n[L136] - Away: Gerrit Cole (R) - ERA 3.67, WHIP 1.13, K9 9.13\n[L137] - Home: Eduardo Rodriguez (L) - ERA 2.62, WHIP 1.22, K9 6.81\n[L138] - Moneyline: Yankees -135, Diamondbacks +110\n[L139] - Run Line: Yankees -1.5 (+125), Diamondbacks +1.5 (-155)\n[L140] - Total: 