is that Muse 1.3 or GLM 5.3 Flash attempted.\n\nSo I would characterize it as:\n\n| Dimension | GPT-5.6 Sol |\n|---|---|\n| Grounding | **Excellent** |\n| Restraint | **Excellent** |\n| Uncertainty handling | **Excellent** |\n| Data accuracy | **Excellent** |\n| Gap filling | **Very low** |\n| Individual-game reasoning | **Excellent** |\n| Anomaly hunting | **Good, not elite** |\n| Cross-slate novelty | **Good** |\n| Black Pearl first-pass fit | **Excellent** |\n\n### Where I put it right now\n\n**Top tier.**\n\nAnd the emerging crew gets even clearer:\n\n- **GPT-5.6 Sol** = disciplined senior analyst\n- **Nex Pro** = hard-nosed evidence skeptic\n- **Muse 1.3** = restrained pattern analyst\n- **Grok 4.6** = contradiction auditor\n- **Dots3** = aggressive anomaly hunter\n\nSol’s particular value is that I’d trust it to receive a sparse packet and **not contaminate the starting frame**.\n\nThat is a very different value proposition from “most clever answer.”\n\nAnd interestingly, it confirms something we’ve been learning all night: **the best Black Pearl first-pass model may be the one least desperate to prove how smart it is.**\n\nBring me the last bastard. Then we can actually lay these fuckers across the deck and talk crew architecture.", "text_chars": 3127, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "empty_text_parts": 0, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "b56dc6d6-e66d-40bf-9242-07dcd0d3ac2f", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1789724613.1247222, "updated_at": null, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "model_editable_context", "part_kinds": [], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "empty_text_parts": 0, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "1c956026-3afd-4cc2