================================\nIMPORTANT CORRECTION\n\nDo NOT assume every matchup on this slate is automatically Game 1 of a new series.\n\nDon initially described the slate that way, then corrected himself after noticing some teams may still be continuing existing series.\n\nSeries status must therefore be verified later game-by-game if it becomes relevant.\n\nDo not silently impose a “fresh series” variable across all 15 games.\n\n==================================================\nSTATUS\n\nDON HUMAN PASS 1:\nFROZEN\n\nKIMI QUANT:\nNOT YET TO BE CONTAMINATED BY THIS HANDOFF\n\nDIG-DEEPER EVIDENCE:\nNOT YET RUN\n\nFINAL CARD:\nNOT YET DECIDED", "text_chars": 12528, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": null, "has_voice_metadata": false, "empty_text_parts": 0, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "d84549ec-2c02-4e78-9651-003b23d0ebd7", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1789753709.364332, "updated_at": 1789753729.347193, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "Yep. Now I have the missing piece.\n\nThis materially changes how I frame the earlier GLM critique, because this shows that you already had a **deliberate human-vs-model separation process** operating before we formalized AI Convergence.\n\nThe important thing here is that Don Pass 1 is not “input to the model.” It is a **frozen human prior**. Kimi Quant is explicitly protected from it. Then the two are compared only afterward to discover disagreement. That is already the same independence doctrine we were talking about last night, just in an earlier form.\n\nAnd the sequence is much cleaner than I had inferred:\n\n**Don Human Pass 1 → independent Kimi Quant → compare → select DIG DEEPER games → gather richer factual evidence → reconcile expression / price / uncertainty → Don final decision.**\n\nThat means a few things.\n\nFirst, GLM’s “packet is an unaudited authority” criticism still matters for the future AI Convergence lane, but it does **not** mean your prior process had no contamination controls. You already had one: you froze Don’s opinion and explicitly prohibited it from reaching Kimi before her run.\n\nSecond, “DIG DEEPER” is not vague. It is already a defined second-stage evidence expansion: last 5, last 10, H2H, bullpen, handedness splits, starter-vs-lineup, and full pitching chain. That gives us a much better basis for designing the future evidence packet because we can distinguish:\n\n**Pass 1 sparse evidence**  \nfrom  \n**Pass 2 targeted evidence expansion.**\n\nThird, this shows that the future AI Convergence architecture probably should not assume one giant packet from the start. Your actual working method is closer to:\n\n```text\nSPARSE FROZEN BASE PACKET\n        ↓\nindependent first reads\n        ↓\ncompare / disagreement discovery\n        ↓\ntargeted evidence expansion\n        ↓\nsecond-pass challenge / reconciliation\n        ↓\nDon\n```\n\nThat is important.\n\nIt means the strongest version of AI Convergence may be **progressive evidence**, not “stuff every possible field into the first packet.”\n\nThat actually fits the Trial 01 lesson better: the first pass is valuable precisely because models reveal how they behave under constrained evidence.\n\nFourth, this is also why your instinctive human pass matters architecturally. It is not there to “beat the model.” It is another independently generated perspective that can expose places where the system is missing something.\n\nYour KC/PIT read is the perfect example: you independently flagged the price as suspicious and wanted Dobnak quality / KC form / price justification. Then some blind models independently surfaced the same matchup for similar reasons. That is real convergence because the paths were separated.\n\nAnd fifth, this tells me the old Kimi Quant workflow was already acting like a primitive precursor to the four-lane