RENT`\n- `01_CROSS_SPORT_METHOD`\n- `02_SPORTS`\n- `03_DATA_SUFFICIENCY`\n- `04_USER_PRODUCT_LOOP`\n- `90_PROVENANCE_ARCHIVE`\n\nThat is good. The current Quant index and sport-status matrix are sitting exactly where I would expect them, and MLB/NFL are separated underneath `02_SPORTS`. The NFL folder already has the September 20 methodology/build handoff material. The archive has the old closeouts, candidate seal, old bootstraps, and cleanup history. So **Quant itself is organized.**\n\nThe structural gap is the work we created in *this* conversation. Right now Drive does **not** yet have clean current homes for the other three Edge Crew verticals or the Black Pearl/model-lab evidence.\n\nI would not disturb the working Quant layout. Instead, I would add four sibling folders at the `01_Edge_Crew` level using numbers that do not collide with the existing Quant internals:\n\n```text\nGCE\n└── 03_Projects\n    └── 01_Edge_Crew\n        ├── 00_EC8_QUANT_CURRENT\n        ├── 01_CROSS_SPORT_METHOD\n        ├── 02_SPORTS\n        ├── 03_DATA_SUFFICIENCY\n        ├── 04_USER_PRODUCT_LOOP\n        │\n        ├── 10_EC_AI_CONVERGENCE\n        ├── 20_EC_MATRIX\n        ├── 30_EC_COMMITTEE_SHIP\n        ├── 40_MODEL_LAB_BLACK_PEARL\n        │\n        ├── 90_PROVENANCE_ARCHIVE\n        └── EC8   ← legacy / historical estate for reconciliation\n```\n\nThat is the smallest change that respects the structure you already built.\n\n### What belongs where\n\n**`10_EC_AI_CONVERGENCE`**\ngets the new AI Convergence scope, handoff, eventual packet contract, prompt contracts, validation artifacts, and current V1/V2 architecture.\n\n**`20_EC_MATRIX`**\ngets the Matrix business/design brief, GLM 5.3 weighting/perspective work, Pete's Matrix concepts, and eventually matrix versions/calibration.\n\n**`30_EC_COMMITTEE_SHIP`**\ngets only the persistent Committee/Ship concept and future work. Keep it thin until it earns implementation.\n\n**`40_MODEL_LAB_BLACK_PEARL`**\nis important. This is where the model audition evidence should live:\nTrial 01 frozen packet, prompt, model outputs/results, labor map, provider/runtime notes, validation backlog, and the Black Pearl workbook. That keeps the **evidence that produced the architecture** separate from the architecture itself.\n\nThat separation is worth preserving.\n\n### One significant legacy issue\n\nThere is already an old:\n\n`EC8 → 00_AI_Convergence_Project_Knowledge_Base`\n\nwith the September 6 AI Convergence charter, runtime designs, old Kimi boundaries, source-discipline docs, handoffs, etc.\n\nI would **not treat that as current** and I would definitely not start dropping our new AI Convergence work in there.\n\nThat folder is valuable historical provenance from the old EC3/EC4 era. Eventually it should either remain clearly under `EC8` as legacy or be reconciled into `90_PROVENANCE_ARCHIVE`. We should read it when designing the new AI lane, but it should not quietly become authority again.\n\n### Loose material I noticed\n\nThere are a few relevant things sitting outside the clean current hierarchy:\n\n- the `EdgeCrew_Quant_WORKING_SPEC_v1.0_DON_APPROVED_2026-09-17.zip` is loose at My Drive root;\n- an older GCE session anchor is loose at root;\n- there are TEMP / delete-later items at root;\n- old Edge Crew backups are correctly living under the frozen/legacy area;\n- a couple of reconciliation/session-header docs currently sit directly in the Edge Crew project root rather than a clearly designated governance/provenance location.\n\nNone of that is an emergency. I would **not clean random root files during this pass**. That becomes a controlled cleanup after we establish the new lane homes.\n\n### Framework side\n\nThe GCE parent itself is also structurally sound:\n\n`GCE`\n→ `GCE_ORG`\n→ `03_Projects`\n→ `06_Frozen_State_and_Archive`\n\n`GCE_ORG` is properly split into Executive Council, Shared Enterprise Services, and Implementation.\n\nThe older Coda/framework anchors live in an existing strategic/governance area, while legacy strategic-advisor material sits under the frozen archive. That is conceptually correct.\n\nSo when we eventually update the framework artifacts from this chat, they should go into the **active GCE governance/framework location**, not into Edge Crew and not into the frozen Strategic Advisor archive.\n\n### My call before we touch documents\n\n**GO on the existing Drive structure with one small extension.**\n\nI would **not reorganize Quant**.\n\nI would create only the four missing Edge Crew vertical homes:\n\n**10 AI Convergence  \n20 Matrix  \n30 Committee/Ship  \n40 Model Lab / Black Pearl**\n\nThen we can inventory the artifacts we produced in this chat and put each one into the correct lane before we update a single document.\n\nThat gives us the architecture in Drive before we start modifying content—which is exactly the right order.", "text_chars": 5103, "code_blocks": 1, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "empty_text_parts": 0, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "c74ab517-a35f-4682-87b6-8ed0835d2d1f", "role": "tool", "role_name": "functions.exec", "created_at": 1790017510.615558, "updated_at": null, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "empty_text_parts": 1, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "9acfddb5-fc34-4a37-9079-09749766128c", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790017518.764421, "updated_at": null, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "thoughts", "part_kinds": [], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_meta