 to GCE framework governance and systems intelligence, not to Projects.** Edge Crew happened to become the proving ground, but the cross-project lessons belong outside the Edge Crew project estate.\n\nAt the Drive level, the canonical framework spine is already strong:\n\n**GCE**\n→ **GCE_ORG**\n→ **01_Executive_Council**\n→ Strategic Governance / Technical Strategy / Operations / Architecture  \n→ **02_Shared_Enterprise_Services**\n→ Data Intelligence / Verification / QA  \n→ **03_Implementation**\n\nAnd separately:\n\n**GCE → 03_Projects → 01_Edge_Crew**\n\nThat separation matches exactly what you just told me: **Projects own project truth; framework owns generalized doctrine, cross-project system intelligence, and governance.**\n\nWhat this chat contributed outside Projects falls into a few clean buckets.\n\n- **Strategic Governance**\n  - MODEL != SEAT reinforcement\n  - stage discipline: POC → Design → Architecture → Validation → Production\n  - authority boundaries\n  - “do not let the architect define an unfinished POC”\n  - one architectural responsibility at a time\n  - preserve disagreement / provenance / evidence\n  - project-to-framework reconciliation rules\n\n- **Technical Strategy / Systems Intelligence**\n  - Black Pearl proving-ground results\n  - model labor map\n  - cognitive-role fit by model\n  - provider/runtime reliability as a separate dimension from reasoning quality\n  - model-family behavior differences\n  - runtime substitution lessons\n  - “right model, right seat”\n  - exploration of mini-crews / role-specialized swarms\n  - this is where the raw Black Pearl research belongs\n\n- **Verification / Ground Truth**\n  - packet-bounded verification concept\n  - Big Pickle / Luce-type truth role lessons\n  - distinction between factual verification and analytical adjudication\n  - verification oracle discipline\n  - external state change → new version, not silent rewrite\n\n- **Framework Standards**\n  - session-stage rules\n  - authority/routing rules\n  - change-control principles\n  - possibly a generalized “evidence independence / convergence” standard later\n  - but only after the lesson graduates from research into canon\n\nAnd this is the important part: **Black Pearl itself should not go into Strategic Governance canon.**\n\nBlack Pearl is evidence.\n\nIt belongs under something like:\n\n`GCE_ORG / 01_Executive_Council / 02_Technical_Strategy_Systems_Intelligence`\n\nThat area is currently almost empty except for `00_Canon_and_Seat_Records`, which actually makes it the perfect place to establish a durable non-project research/intelligence lane.\n\nConceptually, I would eventually want something like:\n\n```text\n02_Technical_Strategy_Systems_Intelligence\n├── 00_Canon_and_Seat_Records\n├── 01_Model_Labor_Intelligence\n├── 02_Runtime_Provider_Intelligence\n├── 03_Proving_Grounds\n└── 04_Cross_Project_Methodology_Research\n```\n\nNot saying create it yet. But that is where this chat naturally maps.\n\n**Black Pearl / Trial 01** would live under `03_Proving_Grounds`.\n\n**Model labor map** would graduate into `01_Model_Labor_Intelligence`.\n\n**OpenRouter/provider reliability / route behavior / runtime identity problems** would live under `02_Runtime_Provider_Intelligence`.\n\nThen only the generalized laws that survive review would move upward into Strategic Governance / Framework Standards.\n\nThat prevents the exact contamination we’ve been trying to avoid:\n\n> experiment ≠ doctrine  \n> observation ≠ canon  \n> project result ≠ framework authority\n\nThe existing Drive manifest already says essentially this: one primary owner, no model-centric top-level folders, no duplicated artifacts, historical provenance preserved, and Projects separated from organizational authority. So the structure you already made was anticipating exactly this problem.\n\nThere’s another important reconciliation.\n\nThe old **Aegis** and **Capo AI** anchors already contain several ideas we rediscovered in Black Pearl in a more concrete form: preserve provenance, convergence without committee mush, authority separate from capability, externalized state, verification at stage gates, exploration before formalization, and controlled promotion from project work into generalized substrate.\n\nSo Black Pearl did **not** create a competing architecture.\n\nIt gave us empirical evidence for some of those framework instincts.\n\nThat means our job is not to create a whole new framework branch called “Black Pearl.”\n\nOur job is:\n\n> preserve Black Pearl as technical-strategy evidence → extract lessons → reconcile them against Aegis/Capo/GCE doctrine → promote only what survives.\n\nThat’s the clean move.\n\nThe other thing I confirmed is that **Framework Standards** is already built for this kind of promotion path. You have folders for Controlled Vocabulary, Session Standards, Authority and Routing, Change Control, Session Lifecycle, Terminology Crosswalk, etc. So when a Black Pearl lesson becomes canon, it has somewhere correct to go.\n\nExample:\n\nBlack Pearl evidence says:\n> different models do different jobs.\n\nThat raw evidence stays in Technical Strategy.\n\nThe generalized framework law might become:\n> seat assignment must be based on demonstrated task-fit and failure signature; model identity alone does not establish suitability.\n\nThat law belongs in Framework Standards / Authority and Routing or Canon and Protocols.\n\nSame pattern for:\n> provider reliability is separate from cognitive capability.\n\nEvidence stays in runtime intelligence.\n\nGeneralized law becomes:\n> runtime/provider operational suitability must be evaluated independently from cognitive suitability.\n\nThat can become standard.\n\nAnd the same applies to the POC-stage lesson.\n\nThe story:\n> we were fucking around with Black Pearl, fed GLM too early, and it started architecting unfinished work.\n\nThat story stays in provenance.\n\nThe framework law:\n> architecture review begins only after exploratory work is explicitly promoted from POC/discovery to design-ready state.\n\nThat belongs in framework lifecycle/change-control doctrine.\n\nSo my recon call is:\n\n**Do not touch Projects.**\n\n**Do not make Black Pearl its own GCE project.**\n\n**Treat this chat as a Strategic Governance + Technical Strategy research/reconciliation source.**\n\nAnd then use a promotion model:\n\n```text\nPROJECT / POC / CHAT EVIDENCE\n        ↓\nTechnical Strategy / Proving Ground\n        ↓\nCross-project reconciliation\n        ↓\nStrategic Governance review\n        ↓\nFramework Standard / Canon\n```\n\nThat is the architecture I would use for cleaning this chat into Drive.\n\nAnd it fits the system you already built rather than inventing another taxonomy. memcite", "text_chars": 6766, "code_blocks": 2, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "empty_text_parts": 0, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "509b5d9d-ceea-47c8-9fa2-74e0ea5d3f7c", "role": "tool", "role_name": "functions.exec", "created_at": 1790018054.181438, "updated_at": null, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "empty_text_parts": 1, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "e72d2be4-7a23-4d1a-aa93-8131f3553473", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790018056.670297, "updated_at": null, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "thoughts", "part_kinds": [], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "empty_text_parts": 0, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "8a3128eb-0894-42c2-b5ff-14f5a7e4e882", 